    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **68 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner resource. Since the DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec at build time, the change spans three files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `ownerSegment` property to the `OwnerDto` schema as a read-only string enum with the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), documenting the TIER/AREA rules.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/Localities.java`** \u2014 Added `segmentForOwner(Owner)`, which computes:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `Owner.effectiveMembershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the owner's derived locality (`forOwner`) is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`. It reuses the existing region key set for the \"known region\" check.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment`, wrapping the helper's string in `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(...)` (matching the existing `ageBand` pattern).\n\nThe reused `effectiveMembershipLevel` and `forOwner` helpers keep the logic consistent with the existing `membershipLevel`, `locality`, and `timezone` derivations. Both new tests in `Cp55Tests` pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
